WEBVTT

00:02:58.796 --> 00:03:01.476
And so we were never
going to get to equality

00:03:01.516 --> 00:03:03.596
until we started fixing the structure.

00:03:03.596 --> 00:03:04.756
And quite frankly,

00:03:04.796 --> 00:03:09.956
I think the abortion debate is part
of that structural conversation.

00:03:09.996 --> 00:03:13.516
You don't give control over women's ...

00:03:13.516 --> 00:03:17.556
you know, about their ability
how and when to have a child,

00:03:17.596 --> 00:03:22.516
you take away their ability,
quite frankly, to work on their terms.

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:26.076
Whitney Pennington Rodgers: What is
the "Marshall Plan for Moms"

00:03:26.076 --> 00:03:27.796
and where are we right now with it?

00:03:27.836 --> 00:03:30.196
RS: We need the government
and the private sector,